\section{Architecture and controlled factors}
Fusion v2 predicts an interpretable residual from persistence. It provides
short (six samples at five minutes), medium (12 samples at 15 minutes), and
slow (24 samples at 60 minutes) Cn²/weather branches; horizon Fourier features;
causal temporal blocks; optional FiLM and cross-attention weather interaction;
four routed experts; physical refractivity/stability tokens; ordered
quantiles; a learned Student-t scale; and OOD diagnostics.

Only one factor changed inside each preregistered category: context, fusion
mechanism, physics tokens, pretraining, capacity/regularization, or probability
calibration. Controls used the same endpoints and fold-only preprocessing.
LightGBM is diagnostic only.

